  "chitchat": [
    "She moves a card tower a quarter-inch and steps back to look at it.",
    "\"Every plot sells twice. Once off the plan and once when it is finished. The trick is the gap.\"",
    "She does not look at the amber pins. It looks like practice."
  ],
  "description": "A tall woman in a pale suit with a laser pointer in her breast pocket like a pen. She is the Director of Land, and she stands at the model the way other people stand at a window.",
  "dialogue_tree": {
    "bye": {
      "options": [],
      "text": "She goes back to the model."
    },
    "model": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Halcyon Fields. Sixty-odd buildings on what used to be allotments and a gas works.\" She runs the pointer along a street of white card. \"Every street is a meadow plant. Buyers like a meadow. Nobody has ever asked to live on Gasworks Lane.\""
    },
    "pins": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Back.",
          "next": "root"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"Plots.\" A short pause. \"Each one is a building that sold before it was finished and is now waiting for the market to remember it. They will all complete.\" She says it the way people say grace."
    },
    "root": {
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "What is all this?",
          "next": "model"
        },
        {
          "label": "What are the amber pins?",
          "next": "pins"
        },
        {
          "label": "Just looking.",
          "next": "bye"
        }
      ],
      "text": "\"You will be from the estate, or you are lost.\" She does not take her eyes off the model."
    }
  },
